Abstract = {The contemporary Jachymov, a small spa town in KruSne hory in the Czech
   Republic, has always had an important role in the country's economy.
   Among the many ores in the Jachymov deposit, silver and uranium have
   been most important. The discovery of silver ores attracted many people
   in the past, and soon one of the biggest towns in the country was
   established. The history of the town is connected with many famous
   scientists interested in inanimate nature, who either visited Jachymov
   or lived there. Among the greatest personalities connected with the
   history of Jachymov, there is Georgius Agricola and Marie
   Curie-Sklodowska. From the historical point of view, Jachymov aspires to
   become an important centre of global geotourism in the future.},
