   International-Association-for-Engineering-Geology-and-the-Environment,
   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {Old mining activities during colonial times have led to the development
   of instability processes in several areas of the Serra de Ouro Preto,
   northern boundary of the urban zone of the city of Ouro Preto. During
   the last twenty years, many landslide and rock fall prone areas have
   been populated as a consequence of the unbridled development of the
   city. Piedade neighborhood borough is a typical example of such a
   situation. The use of old mining areas has caused high hazard situations
   for the population. Geologic studies have been done to identify current
   processes, analyze major events and their consequences, and assess the
   geologic hazard due to mass movements. A hazard map of the study area
   has been produced and it is shown in this work.},
