   Bohemia Ltd},
Abstract = {The impact of land-use change impacts on runoff generation is presented
   based on a study composed of generation of spatially explicit land-use
   conditions in part of Kosice City, catchment of Myslavsky creek. We were
   analyzed the drainage conditions of river basin Myslavsky creek in the
   paper. Drainage conditions of the reference area were compared on the
   basis of two time periods, for year 1980 and for 2010. Two maps of land
   use area were processed for the both years. Total runoff coefficients
   were calculated based on processed maps, which differed, because in 1980
   the territory was not so built as currently. Today the situation is
   different, because in 30 years the enormously increased number of built
   and paved areas and all rainwater is collected and discharged through
   rainwater drainage discharges into the watercourse Myslavsky creek.
   Rainwater from new built objects, mainly hypermarkets, increases the
   flow in Myslavsky creek, and thus its flow capacity for amount of
   drained rainwater is poor.},
