Abstract = {The paper discussed the influence of unsteady wind characteristic on
   efficiency of natural ventilation, and introduced the limitation of
   evaluating ventilation efficiency under traditional steady boundary
   condition (Hereinafter referred to as ``B/C{''}) of wind. The paper also
   chiefly reviewed current methods and tools employed in natural
   ventilation study. A visualized wind tunnel experiment was carried out
   and two types of B/Cs were generated in the experiment. The ventilation
   efficiency distinction between them was clearly observed. A small-sized
   automatic weather station was established in an urban area and
   continuous data of city wind was measured from April to August. In CFD
   simulation, two cases of B/C of wind were input. One was the objective
   wind data with variational wind speed and direction, the other case was
   the wind data with mean speed and at the prevailing direction. According
   to these investigations, the paper introduced the error results from
   evaluating ventilation with steady B/C. Finally, the paper introduced
   the prospective work, looking forward developing more accurate and
   efficient evaluation and prediction methods of natural ventilation.},
