   and Prospects, Sibiu, ROMANIA, JUN 03-05, 2011},
Abstract = {The affection of central nervous system within the infection VHC was
   evaluated through different methods. In this study I followed the degree
   of depression, satisfaction in life, the wellbeing and the life quality
   in comparison at the patients with kidney transplant and the patients
   with dialysis, who have VHC-infection. I applied questionnaires
   well-known in the literature of speciality. The depression, although
   presented in the both parts, was more accentuated to the patients with
   hemodialysis. The wellbeing, which reflects the balance of the
   activities from the patients' lives, is moderate at both of the groups.
   The satisfaction in life, integrative reflection of the person's
   reporting at his/her past, present or future, is moderate for both of
   the categories, but superior to the patients with kidney transplant. In
   conclusion, there exists the possibility that this infection with virus
   of hepatitis C, to influence the neuro-psychical activity of the
   patients with chronic renal failure, more stressed for the patients with
   dialysis than to those with kidney transplant.},
