Note = {3rd International Conference on Urban Transport and the Environment for
   the 21st Century (UT 97), ACQUASPARTA, ITALY, SEP, 1997},
Organization = {Univ Perugia; Wessex Inst Technol},
Abstract = {As rapid economic development takes place? intense vehicle use from
   motorization and suburbanization becomes a crucial contributor to energy
   consumption and environmental degradation Without proper measures to
   control traffic congestion, the benefits from increasing mobility would
   be swiftly dissipated particularly for developing cities. Sprawl pattern
   in suburban areas with scattered housing settlement and poor public
   transport services encourage longer trip distance and frequent car trips
   thereby much larger energy use in these cities. How successful to
   mitigate the problems depends on the extent of government intervention
   to vehicle ownership, land use control, and provision of efficient
   public transport services.},
