Title = {Application of fractal theory in typhoon storm surge simulation},
Booktitle = {2008 PROCEEDINGS OF INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY AND ENVIRONMENTAL SYSTEM
   SCIENCES: ITESS 2008, VOL 3},
Year = {2008},
Pages = {812-815},
Note = {International Conference on Informational Technology and Environmental
   System Science, Henan Polytechn Univ, Jiaozuo, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY
   15-17, 2008},
Abstract = {Storm Surge is one kind of serious natural disasters coming from the
   sea, for the sudden reduction in atmospheric pressure and following
   strong winds, it often brings huge damage to coastal regions. For the
   topographic influence, typhoon storm surge became a main oceanic
   disaster in the south of China. To better illustrate the potential
   impact of these violent weather phenomenon on the nature and
   people's,lives, many systems have been developed for the simulation of
   typhoon storm surge. Geographic information system is an effective tool
   to visualize temporal and spatial processes and to analyze spatial data.
   However, the existing visual means in typhoon simulation are most static
   images, simply animations or videos, which are either less realistic or
   much difficult in being used in GIS. A fractal based typhoon storm surge
   model is proposed in the paper. It uses the fractal technology to form
   the contour of typhoon according to a given time, space, wind speed and
   central pressure, at the same time, with the forecasting data of water
   changes along the coast, a realistic parameterized virtual typhoon storm
   surge was formed. Using a 2d or 3d Logarithmic Spiral model and a simple
   topographic model, the basic typhoon shape and sea surface can be
   generated, and then, they will be deformed with the successive random
   addition method. To keep the continuity of shape, positions of different
   time were interpolated. The data of typhoon storm surge along Fujian
   coast in 2006 was taken as the working substance to do the
   visualization. The results showed that this method could generate
   realistic typhoon shapes and was less time expensive and easy to build
   view dependent LOD model.},
