Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol},
Abstract = {The Adelaide Taxi Industry Baseline Study (ATIBS96) was conducted
   throughout 1996 to collect a variety of statistics of interest to
   members of the industry and to policy-makers. The first of a planned
   series of follow-up studies was conducted in 1998 (ATIS98). Though the
   1998 effort was less extensive than ATIBS96, it enabled comparisons of
   the key operational characteristics of the industry. Of particular
   interest were the proportions of the means of engagement of the jobs;
   the quality of service with regard to passengers (waiting times and rank
   queues); the ratios of active versus non-active time and distance
   travelled for taxis; and the revenue per trip, per shift etc. This paper
   compares the statistics derived from each study and briefly describes
   the methodologies of the data collection and analysis.
   The opinions presented are those of the authors and should not be
   regarded as those of the Passenger Transport Board of South Australia.},
