   Health, Guilin, PEOPLES R CHINA, MAY 29-31, 2009},
Organization = {Hunan Univ; Univ Hong Kong; Tsinghua Univ},
Abstract = {In this paper, energy consumption of public buildings in Changsha,
   Wuhan, Dongguan, Guangzhou and Hainan province is compared and analyzed
   systemly. It indicates that the mean energy consumption per unit area in
   Southern China is lower than that in Northern China, and the energy
   consumption in Guangzhou is highest and lowest in Wuhan among Southern
   cities because of different geographical location, urban development,
   building energy-saving design and management. Based on existed surveys
   of many institutes, 41 public buildings from Southern cities are chosen
   to analyze the mean energy consumption per unit area and the energy
   consumption proportion of air-conditioning in Southern China. According
   to the Statistics Principle, energy consumption of public building per
   unit area in southern China is 1.765 GJ/(m(2).a), with Confidence
   Interval {[}1.590, 1.947] GJ/(m(2).a) when the Confidence Degree is 0.2.
   Energy consumption of air-conditioning accounts for 44.33\% of the total
   building energy consumption, with Confidence Interval {[}41.34, 47.33]
   when the Confidence Degree is 0.05. The relative errors are acceptable
   and the results we get are reasonable and valuable.},
