   Environm Technol SA},
Abstract = {There are important functional relationships between river basins and
   coastal areas and one may influence the other. The two systems are
   linked through natural processes (water flow, sediment transport,
   energy) and human activities (urban development, rural activities,
   technical infrastructures, waste and pollution).
   The coastal zone is an essential part of a river basin. Both, river
   basin and coastal problems require a multisectoral approach. In some
   cases the two systems require a common framework of management. The
   goals, general objectives and principles of integrated river basin and
   coastal zone management are discussed.},
