   (GEOENVIRONMENT 97), MELBOURNE, AUSTRALIA, NOV 26-28, 1997},
Organization = {Austr Geomech Soc; New Zealand Geotech Soc; Inst Engineers Austr; Int
   Soc Soil Mech \& Geotech Engn},
Abstract = {Increasing population in the Illawarra coastal region, some 100 km south
   of Sydney, is leading to the transformation of large areas from rural
   dairying to urban residential land use. To allow proper planning
   guidelines to be put into place, a selected catchment, Cooback Creek, is
   being monitored before, during, and after urban development. Continuous
   recording of stream turbidity is being supplemented by stage sampling of
   water from the stream. The stage samples are analysed for a full range
   of water quality parameters. This paper describes the initial phases of
   the project and provides details of the catchment and instrumentation
   installed. Preliminary water quality analyses are also presented.},
