   International-Association-for-Engineering-Geology-and-the-Environment,
   VANCOUVER, CANADA, SEP 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Int Assoc Engn Geol \& Environm},
Abstract = {This paper presents the results of an investigation into an engineering
   geological information system for land-use planning in South Africa.
   Rapid urbanisation has resulted in the critical need to find suitable
   land for new urban development. A key issue in the land identification
   process is the finding of geotechnically suitable land. There is a need
   for a system that can store all related information in a systematic and
   logical structure for the compilation of thematic engineering geological
   maps. During the research the Pretoria - Johannesburg region was
   selected and a number of data layers, such as geology, landform and
   geotechnical properties were compiled. Data was collected at a scale of
   1:10 000 and stored in the GIS. Through a process of querying, the
   available data was evaluated in terms of development potential and
   capability to accommodate various land-uses.},
