Year = {2024},
Pages = {177-182},
Note = {2024 International Conference on Energy and Environment-ICEE-Bringing
   together Engineering and Economics, Guimaraes, PORTUGAL, JUN 06-07, 2024},
Abstract = {Owing to the considerable increase in waste production in recent years,
   the management of municipal solid waste (MSW) in Brazil has become a
   significant challenge for the government. Since 2010, the Brazilian
   government has invested resources in establishing policies and guides to
   encourage the creation of integrated waste management plans by
   municipalities and states. In this context, the objective of this study
   is to perform an environmental assessment of different scenarios and
   urban solid waste management systems applicable in the Greater ABC
   region in Brazil, using the methodology of life cycle analysis (LCA).
   Five scenarios were analysed, varying the percentage of separation of
   recyclable materials and organic fractions. In each scenario, hybrid
   configurations were studied, integrating different technologies:
   landfill with (LGR) and without gas recovery (LF), anaerobic
   biodigestion (AD) with electricity generation, recycling (RCY), and
   energy recovery through combustion (ER). Among the management systems
   studied, the hybrid configuration that showed the best results, when
   compared to the current scenario, in the climate change, ozone
   depletion, human toxicity and freshwater categories was made up of RCY,
   A.D and LGR.},
