Note = {10th Regional IUAPPA Conference, ISTANBUL, TURKEY, SEP 23-26, 1997},
Organization = {IUAPPA},
Abstract = {Air quality continues to be one of the most evident impacts in the
   formation of urban metropolises or mega-cities. Exposure to elevated
   concentrations of ambient air pollutants causes adverse human health
   effects. In addition to the criteria gaseous and particulate air
   pollutant, a number of toxic contaminants exists in the atmosphere of
   cities and surrounding areas which are related to public health and
   regulatory concern. One of the facilities which release toxic air
   contaminants into the atmosphere are excessive industrialization and
   accordingly industrial wastewater treatment plant. The emissions of
   volatile organic carbons (VOCs) such as carbon tetra chloride,
   1,3-butadiene, ethylene oxide and trichloroethylene are carcinogen and
   mutagen for human health due to the Office of Environmental Health
   Hazard Assessment in USA.
   The aim of this search are identify the toxic VOCs originated from
   industrial wastewater treatment plants, to emphasize the serious effects
   to human health to control and to promote some control technologies by
   providing a protection level.},
