Abstract = {The purpose of this paper is to present a coalition based multi-agent
   model for the Vehicle Routing Problem with Time Windows, which is one of
   the most important ones in distribution and transportation. The VRPTW
   objective is to design least cost routes from one depot to a set of
   customers. A fleet of homogeneous vehicles performs the routes to serve
   all the customers, while respecting capacity and time window
   constraints.
   The proposed model is detailed, illustrated through a numerical example,
   experimented on the base of Solomon s benchmark and compared to the
   optimal solution.},
