   MAR 28-30, 2007},
Organization = {IWA; Dokuz Eylul Univ, Environm Engn Dept; Middle E Tech Univ Turkey},
Abstract = {Thermal treatments with temperature ranging from 60 to 210 degrees C
   were applied to 6 waste-activated sludge samples originating from high
   or medium load, extended aeration wastewater treatment processes that
   treated different wastewaters (urban, urban and industrial or
   slaughterhouse). COD sludge solubilisation was linearly correlated with
   the treatment temperature on the whole temperature range and
   independently of the sludge samples. Sludge batch mesophilic
   biodegradability increased with treatment temperature up to 190 degrees
   C. In this temperature range, biodegradability enhancement or methane
   production increase by thermal hydrolysis was shown to be a function of
   sludge COD solubilisation but also of sludge initial biodegradability.
   The lower the initial biodegradability means the higher efficiency of
   thermal treatment.},
