   NOV 21-24, 1998},
Organization = {Decis Sci Inst},
Abstract = {An organization's reputation for risk-taking has a significant impact on
   its relationships with its stakeholders. We identify key components of a
   firm's reputation for risk-taking and measure the relative importance of
   each component in managers' perception of the risk orientation of a
   firm. Perceptions of a firm's culture/leadership,
   innovation/environmental fit, firm's culture/leadership, public
   visibility, and acquisition strategy collectively explain a significant
   proportion of the variance in perception of the risk orientation of the
   firm. Conclusions and directions for future research and practice are
   discussed.},
