Organization = {Wessex Inst Technol; Advances Transport Book Series},
Abstract = {Transportation in Mongolia is not sufficient to meet the requirement for
   modernization of the country. To improve it, a huge amount of
   construction of infrastructure is necessary. Its cost is many times
   larger than that citizens can bare. We need a new method of
   transportation in Mongolia. The necessary items of the new method are a)
   high speed to cover a large area of the land, b) low cost without a
   large scale of infrastructure and c) easy to operate, repair and
   maintenance. Wing-In-Surface-Effect craft is a hopeful method of
   transportation. It can fly at 1-3 m altitude at a speed of 150-400 km/h.
   The present authors started a joint project between Japan and Mongolia
   to realize a Wing-In-Surface-Effect craft in Mongolia, being financially
   supported by the Heiwa-Nakajima Foundation. They report the present
   state of their study.},
